acceptance_criteria: "The five 2026-07-16 unknown-author test_run_track events carry an audited acknowledgment with reviewer, attributed author, and reason, recorded without rewriting history or moving the baseline; pm health returns ok:true and validate no longer reports validate_history_unknown_author_events for this workspace; acknowledgeUnknownAuthorHistoryEvents is reachable from the CLI and from MCP with the same typed errors as the SDK primitive, wired through every required registration site; Docs state when acknowledgment is appropriate and that it is a recorded disposition, never a way to attribute authorship after the fact"
goal: provable-history
objective: "Every validate and health warning maps to an open item, and the acknowledgment capability is reachable without writing SDK code"
value: "The acknowledgment flow shipped as an SDK primitive and was never run against this repository, so pm health has reported ok:false continuously since 2026-07-16 and the workspace's own governance signal is permanently degraded."
impact: "Restores health to a trustworthy binary signal instead of a known-red one that reviewers learn to ignore, and removes the last validate warning with no open owner."
outcome: "The five stranded events carry an audited disposition, pm health returns ok:true, and acknowledgment is invocable from the CLI and MCP rather than only from TypeScript."
why_now: "The attribution-enforcement item closed on the strength of the primitive existing; the repo-side execution half was never scheduled, which is the same shipped-but-not-adopted pattern the merge-safety adoption work already hit once."
